 sequenceDiagram
  participant U as User
  participant F as Frontend
  participant B as Backend
  participant P as Payment Provider
  participant DB as Supabase/Postgres
  participant E as Email Service
  participant S as Shipper

  %% Browsing and cart
  U->>F: Browse products & add to cart
  F->>DB: Save/Update cart (cart rows)
  DB-->>F: OK

  %% Checkout flow
  U->>F: Checkout (submit order request)
  F->>B: POST /payments/orders { cart, address, phone }
  B->>DB: Create order (status: pending) + order_items
  DB-->>B: order row

  %% Payment session
  B->>P: Create payment session (gateway API)
  P-->>B: payment_url / session_id
  B-->>F: return payment_url
  F->>U: redirect user to payment provider

  %% User completes payment at provider
  U->>P: Complete payment (approve/authorize)
  P-->>B: (webhook) send payment notification
  B->>P: Verify webhook signature / validate event
  P-->>B: verification OK

  %% Finalize order after payment
  B->>DB: Insert payment row, update order.status = 'paid'
  DB-->>B: OK
  B->>E: Send order confirmation email to user
  E-->>B: OK
  B-->>F: (optional) push realtime update / emit websocket event

  alt payment failed
    P-->>B: webhook (failed)
    B->>DB: update order.status = 'failed' or 'cancelled'
    B->>E: notify user of failure
  end

  %% Fulfillment & shipping (admin/auto)
  A->>B: Admin confirms & processes order (optional)
  B->>S: Create shipment request (optional)
  S-->>B: tracking_id
  B->>DB: update order.status = 'shipped', add tracking
  B->>E: send shipment email (with tracking)

  %% User views order and delivery
  U->>F: View Orders page
  F->>B: GET /orders (authenticated)
  B->>DB: SELECT order, order_items, payments, tracking
  DB-->>B: order data
  B-->>F: return order details
  F-->>U: display order + tracking

  %% Post-delivery and feedback
  U->>F: After delivery, leave feedback / review
  F->>B: POST /reviews (Authorization: Bearer <token>)
  B->>DB: Verify user has a PAID order with product -> insert review
  DB-->>B: inserted review
  B-->>F: success

  %% Optional flows: refund / return
  U->>B: Request refund/return
  B->>DB: update order.status = 'refund_pending'
  B->>P: Initiate refund via payment provider
  P-->>B: refund status
  B->>DB: update order.status = 'refunded' / record refund
  B->>E: notify user

  note right of B: Server uses service-role key for inserts/updates
  note left of U: Reviews only accepted after purchase (enforced by backend)
